From: nuno407 <11352538+nuno407@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:10:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 38/45] driver core: fw_devlink: a probed consumer needs no
 sync-state link

When a parent device that supplies its own child's device-less graph
nodes binds, fw_devlink picks up those dangling consumers and asks for
a SYNC_STATE_ONLY proxy link from the child device. If the child probed
first (tegra-video: the VI populates its CSI child, which probes before
the VI finishes), device_link_add() refuses the link by design, and
fw_devlink logged it as an error:

  tegra-csi 54080800.csi: Failed to create device link (0x180) with
  supplier 54080000.vi for /host1x@50000000/vi@54080000/csi@800/channel@1

A sync-state-only link only matters until the consumer probes; skip it
then.
---
 drivers/base/core.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/base/core.c b/drivers/base/core.c
index 4d0266829..ce358def2 100644
--- a/drivers/base/core.c
+++ b/drivers/base/core.c
@@ -2236,6 +2236,22 @@ static int fw_devlink_create_devlink(struct device *con,
 			goto out;
 		}
 
+		/*
+		 * A SYNC_STATE_ONLY link only matters until the consumer has
+		 * probed, and device_link_add() refuses one after that. That
+		 * is no failure: it happens when a child device probes before
+		 * its parent, the supplier, finishes probing, and the parent's
+		 * dangling consumers (the child's device-less graph nodes)
+		 * are picked up as it binds.
+		 */
+		if (flags & DL_FLAG_SYNC_STATE_ONLY &&
+		    con->links.status != DL_DEV_NO_DRIVER &&
+		    con->links.status != DL_DEV_PROBING) {
+			dev_dbg(con, "Not linking %pfwf - consumer already probed\n",
+				sup_handle);
+			goto out;
+		}
+
 		if (con != sup_dev && !device_link_add(con, sup_dev, flags)) {
 			dev_err(con, "Failed to create device link (0x%x) with supplier %s for %pfwf\n",
 				flags, dev_name(sup_dev), link->consumer);
-- 
